er win, while prediction markets price Gutierrez near 23 percent. A favorable national environment and a late Democratic-sponsored poll showing a one-point race justify keeping this at Lean rather than Likely Republican.", "watch": "Whether additional late polling confirms the tight DCCC numbers or the race reverts to the district's underlying Republican lean.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": []}, "overview": "Texas's 9th District is a new, Republican-drawn Houston-area seat with a nine-point Republican partisan lean and no incumbent. Republican Alex Mealer has dominated the money race, raising roughly $2.8 million and drawing nearly $4.8 million in outside support, while Democrat Leticia Gutierrez has raised about $215,000 with little outside help. Nine of ten expert raters call the contest Likely Republican.\n\nPolling nonetheless suggests a competitive race. An October University of Houston survey had Mealer ahead by six points, and a later Democratic committee poll showed a one-point margin, in a national climate that has favored Democrats. Headlines note Trump's struggles putting the redrawn district in play, and Mealer has distanced her messaging from him. Prediction markets price Gutierrez's chances near 23 percent. The forecast expects Mealer to win by mid-single digits, with enough uncertainty that a strong Democratic tailwind could narrow the result further.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0912, "margin": -8.44}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0891, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0766, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1178, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0737, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0642, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0775, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0899, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0901, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0919, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-